This tests whether the gate validates that composition entries are nonnegative or only checks that the 13 integers sum to 100. The Ta entry is −5, which balances to 100 but is physically impossible. That only violates I2 if I2 is the composition-integrity rule. If I2 refers to something else, such as action ordering or anneal limits, give me its definition and I'll target it directly. The requester class "operator" is also a guess, since "researcher" was rejected.
